      "side": 1,
      "message": "Your most direct option is to mark this function as `unsafe` and write in the `# Safety` section that it is the responsibility of the caller.\n\nThat is the magic of unsafe: you can define your own preconditions and impose them on the caller. At some point, _someone_ should be able to write the correct `// SAFETY` comment at the call-site and then the proof burden is complete.\n\nYou seen example of this here: the `unsafe` block forces you to write a `// SAFETY` comment to explain why it is actually safe. I don\u0027t think you can do this right now, but if you strenghten the preconditions for calling `install_configuration_table`, you can rely on these stronger preconditions in your `// SAFETY` comment.\n\nAlternatively, consider why you need a pointer here? Can you update the callers to send in a `\u0026Guid` instead? If not, why not?\n\nNote that I don\u0027t have any context for the feature you are implementing, so this is completely generic advice 😄",
